    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nCython 3.3.0 crashes while it infers the type of `.items()` on an optional typed dictionary. Cython 3.2.9 compiles the same file. Master at `ab9899598718f3d949e86aff7d34bdee622ebe72` also crashes.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour\n\n```cython\n# cython: language_level=3, annotation_typing=False\n\ndef iterate_optional_dict(values: dict[int, float] | None = None):\n    for key, value in (values or {}).items():\n        pass\n```\n\n```console\npython -m cython repro.py -o repro.c\n```\n\nThe compiler raises `TypeError: NoneType object is not iterable` in `SimpleCallNode.infer_type`.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCython creates the C file, as Cython 3.2.9 does.\n\n### Environment\n\n- OS: Ubuntu on WSL\n- Python: 3.12\n- Cython: 3.3.0 and master",
